The {{Term/Store|Phantom Helmet|Phantom Helmets|Series, BotW, TotK}} is a recurring [[Item]] in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK}}<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Descriptions BotW}}
The Phantom Helmet is a piece of Armor exclusive to ''[[The Master Trials]]'' DLC Pack. Obtaining it is one part of the objective of the "[[EX Treasure: Phantasma]]" [[Side Quest]]. The Helmet was stolen from [[Hyrule Castle (Dungeon)|Hyrule Castle]] by [[Misko]] and a clue to its location can be found in ''[[Misko's EX Journal]]'' at the [[Outpost Ruins]].<ref name="BotW Misko's EX Journal"/><ref name="BotW Misko's EX Journal 2"/> The [[Treasure Chest]] that hides the Phantom Helmet can be found buried near a wall on the first floor of the [[Coliseum Ruins]]. After obtaining the Phantom Helmet, [[Granté]] will begin selling it for 50 Rupees.{{Note|Prior to the {{Version|BotW|1.3.3}}, Granté would not sell any Armor that is exclusive to the Expansion Pass or The Master Trials DLC Pack. This meant that the Phantom Helmet could not be replaced if sold, which was noted in the description of the Helmet.<ref name="BotW Inventory 2"/> The Phantom Helmet's description was changed in the {{Version|BotW|1.3.3}} Update as the Helmet could now be replaced.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/>}} According to its description, the Phantom Helmet looks just like the Helmets supposedly worn by [[Phantom]]s that tormented heroes.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> When worn, the Helmet provides one level of [[Attack Up]]. The Phantom Helmet cannot be enhanced by a [[Great Fairy]] nor can it be [[Dye]]d at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]]. The Phantom Helmet, alongside the [[Phantom Armor]] and [[Phantom Greaves]], compose the [[Phantom Equipment]].

